    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN report confirms a global-buffer-overflow READ of size 2 at the exact location — `string_as_int16` in `parse_headers` at `lwan-request.c:541`, reading 0 bytes past the right edge of the `data_copy` global variable.\n\nThe input is a 32767-byte buffer that starts with a PROXY v2 LOCAL header (whose signature `\\r\\n\\r\\n...` satisfies the finalizer), followed by a `GET / HTTP/1.1\\r\\n` request line, then a very long header line (32732 bytes of padding) ending with `\\r\\n`, and finally a lone `\\r` at the last byte. When `parse_headers` reaches that trailing `\\r`, the `STRING_SWITCH_SMALL` macro reads 2 bytes via `string_as_int16`, but only 1 byte remains in the buffer — causing the overflow.",
